edb/ref 17592186108997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-47220" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111212 #edb/ref 1071 "By expressing $\\frac{5}{2}{log}_{2}⁡t$ in the form ${log}_{2}⁡({t}^{k}),$ determine the value of $k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "280546e1-c920-58e1-a384-cc694d6876d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111212 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the power rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡({c}^{m})=m{log}_{n}⁡(c)\n$$\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{log}_{2}⁡t & ={log}_{2}⁡({t}^{5/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence $k=\\frac{5}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111495 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111495 #edb/ref 1061 14483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111495 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "19f59ba1-2dd1-5223-a575-1ac050cc06a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111495 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111496 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111496 #edb/ref 1061 14484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111496 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4b4565b4-8962-5d8d-9738-1643af7b266f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111496 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111497 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111497 #edb/ref 1061 14485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111497 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75d83154-8fc0-574f-a1e0-c849c2b74681" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111497 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111498 #edb/ref 1061 14486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111498 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f5f3bdde-8c4a-5692-9bd4-7cbb12a161ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111498 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111880 #edb/ref 1064 "The **power rule** allows us to simplify logarithms of exponentiated expressions. It states that\n\n$$\n\\log_{n}\\left( c^{\\color{blue}m} \\right) = {\\color{blue}m}\\log_{n}{c}.\n$$\n\nIn other words, the logarithm has the effect of \"bringing down the power.\"\n\nFor example, let's use the rule to simplify $\\log\\left(125\\right)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(125) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({5}^{3}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** To understand why the power rule works, notice that we can reach the same result using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(125) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({5}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(5\\cdot 5\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)+\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)+\\operatorname{log}⁡(5) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe power rule is just a shortcut for the above procedure." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111880 #edb/ref 1065 2795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111880 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3cb8c8f4-3573-58ab-8e08-3c60cc3a3d12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111880 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542649 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542649 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542649 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03a0860c-abf2-5370-b060-96e1084cffd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542677 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542677 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542677 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0fd1cadd-a51e-5998-81c1-fca762ad9165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542684 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542684 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542684 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11f202f0-5a2c-50a9-86a4-8e1f90d2fc6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542770 #edb/ref 1080 "{log}_{2}⁡(7t)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218